# Android release build (`/gradlew-android`)

If the user says **`/gradlew-android`**, **`gradlew-android`**, or asks to build the Android **release APK**, do this (do not invent `/gradlew` paths):

## Correct command (preferred)

From the **repo root**:

```bash
npm run gradlew-android
```

Equivalent:

```bash
npm run gradlew-android --workspace apps/mobile
# or
bash apps/mobile/scripts/gradlew-android.sh
```

## Manual Gradle (only if needed)

```bash
cd apps/mobile/android
./gradlew assembleRelease
```

## Common mistakes to avoid

- `/gradlew` → looks at filesystem root → `zsh: no such file or directory`
- Use **`./gradlew`** (dot-slash) from `apps/mobile/android`
- Task is **`assembleRelease`** (one word), not `assemble release`
- Android project is at **`apps/mobile/android`**, not repo-root `android/`

## Output

APK path:

`apps/mobile/android/app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk`

The script also rebuilds `@nidavellir/shared` and runs `ensure-mobile-node-modules.js` before Gradle.
